{
  "_comment": [
    "Worn, great and laid out long ago, the ground and what stands on it leaning that way, and faded with it, its",
    "builders' works gone to ruin: two of more weathering, a yellowed or grey light, dust in the air, a faint haze,",
    "and old stone underfoot are offered to every ancient Age, each yielding to anything the book says.",
    "",
    "Aimed at the features it crumbles what they build of rock above the ground a little; laid bare, now and then",
    "(Features.CRUMBLE).",
    "",
    "`ancient structures` and `ancient villages` crumble, as they are aimed; an ancient Age leaves its structures whole (R5, Jonah).",
    "",
    "Aimed at the landmass it is the most wear there is, always: more than `worn` (Jonah, 2026-11-07), so an",
    "`ancient archipelagic landmass` is atolls. Laid bare it adds a little wear, now and then."
